This immunoblot (Figure 7D) confirms that Nano-11, when combined with LPS priming, induces the secretion of the active 17 kD form of IL-1β from bone marrow-derived dendritic cells. While the precursor pro-IL-1β (around 30 kD) is observed in cell lysates after LPS priming, the active 17 kD IL-1β is prominently detected in the supernatant only in the presence of both LPS and Nano-11, highlighting Nano-11's role in promoting the biologically active form of this pro-inflammatory cytokine.